      *################################################################*00010099
      *                                                                 00020099
      *                                                                 00030099
      * >>> NB! This copy book is also used outside EDB Core,  <<<      00040099
      * >>> it is also defined in MKS/SubVersion.              <<<      00050099
      * >>> If changes are required, these versions must be    <<<      00060099
      * >>> harmonized. This must be done in co-operation with <<<      00070099
      * >>> those responsible for PO and for iHub!!!           <<<      00080099
      * >>>                       Jan.2009, Henning L. Rødland <<<      00090099
      *                                                                 00100099
      *                                                                 00110099
      *                      EDB Solutions                              00120099
      *                                                                 00130099
      * GSM Error Handling                                              00140099
      *                                                                 00150099
      * Copy-book R791ERR0.                                             00160099
      *                                                                 00170099
      *################################################################*00180099
      *                                                                 00190099
      * What to implement in your program:                              00200099
      *                                                                 00210099
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*00220099
      * Working-Storage:                                                00230099
      *                                                                 00240099
      *    05  WC-Program-ID             Pic  X(08) Value '&program-Id'.00250099
      *                                                                 00260099
      *01  Filler.                                                      00270099
      *    Copy R791ERR0.                                               00280099
      *Copy R791ERRX.                                                   00290099
      *                                                                 00300099
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*00310099
      * Procedure Division - B000-Initialize section:                   00320099
      *                                                                 00330099
      *    Initialize                          R791ERR0-Error-Handling  00340099
      *    Initialize                          R791ERRX-External-Data   00350099
      *                                                                 00360099
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*00370099
      * Procedure Division - at the end of the program:                 00380099
      *                                                                 00390099
      *Copy S791ERR0.                                                   00400099
      *Copy SnnnERRS.  (System specific,                                00410099
      *                 make your own version, based on S791ERRS)       00420099
      *                                                                 00430099
      *Copy S791ERRQ.  (For SQLCA calls, use only in DB2 programs)      00440099
      *Copy S791ERX0.  (Use this only if your program also use R7919999)00450099
      *                                                                 00460099
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*00470099
      * Alt 1a: Abend situation occurs in your program:                 00480099
      *                                                                 00490099
      *      When "something bad happens..."                            00500099
      *        Move  &message-id         To    R791ERR0-In-Message-ID   00510099
      * if message contains variables:                                  00520099
      *        Move  &name               To    R791ERR0-In-Var-Key  (1) 00530099
      *        Move  &value              To    R791ERR0-In-Var-Data (1) 00540099
      * if you've got any keys to share with others:                    00550099
      *        Perform ZKEY-Move-Keys   (see documentation)             00560099
      * if you've got any status-codes to share with others:            00570099
      *        Move  SQLcode             To    R791ERRX-SQL-Code        00580099
      *        Move  DIBstat             To    R791ERRX-DLI-Status      00590099
      *        Move  &file-status        To    R791ERRX-File-Status     00600099
      * mandatory:                                                      00610099
      *        Move  &paragraph-ID       To    R791ERR0-In-Paragraph-Id 00620099
      *        Set   R791ERRX-State-Abend                               00630099
      *        Perform Z600-Error-Handling                              00640099
      *                                                                 00650099
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*00660099
      * Alt 1b: SQL Abend situation occurs in your program:             00670099
      *                                                                 00680099
      *   When you encounter an SQL abend situation, you should send    00690099
      *   the SQLCA to the Error Handling Module.                       00700099
      *   To do this, you need to have the copy area S791ERRQ at the    00710099
      *   bottom of your program.                                       00720099
      *                                                                 00730099
      *   The error handling logic is exactly the same as without SQLCA 00740099
      *   (see alternative 1a), except that instead of performing Z600, 00750099
      *   you should perform:                                           00760099
      *                                                                 00770099
      *        Perform Z700-Error-Handling-SQLCA                        00780099
      *                                                                 00790099
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*00800099
      * Alt 1c: State-Abend upon return from a sub-program:             00810099
      *                                                                 00820099
      *      When R791ERRX-State-Abend                                  00830099
      * if you've got any keys to share with others:                    00840099
      *        Perform ZKEY-Move-Keys   (see documentation)             00850099
      * mandatory:                                                      00860099
      *        Move  &paragraph-ID       To    R791ERR0-In-Paragraph-Id 00870099
      *        Perform Z800-Call-Trace                                  00880099
      *                                                                 00890099
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*00900099
      * Alt 1d: State-Abend upon return from a sub-program,             00910099
      *         where R7919999 is used:                                 00920099
      *                                                                 00930099
      *      When R7919999-Return-Abend                                 00940099
      * if you've got any keys to share with others:                    00950099
      *        Perform ZKEY-Move-Keys   (see documentation)             00960099
      * mandatory:                                                      00970099
      *        Move  &paragraph-ID       To    R791ERR0-In-Paragraph-Id 00980099
      *        Perform Z300-Call-Trace-R7919999                         00990099
      *                                                                 01000099
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*01010099
      * Alt 2a: Error situation occurs in your program:                 01020099
      *                                                                 01030099
      *   Error situations is handled exactly the same way as abend     01040099
      *   situations, except that instead of setting -State-Abend,      01050099
      *   you should:                                                   01060099
      *                                                                 01070099
      *        Set   R791ERRX-State-Error                               01080099
      *                                                                 01090099
      *   See alternative 1a...                                         01100099
      *                                                                 01110099
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*01120099
      * Alt 2b: State-Error upon return from a sub-program:             01130099
      *                                                                 01140099
      *   Error situations is handled exactly the same way as abend     01150099
      *   situations, except that instead of testing on -State-Abend,   01160099
      *   you test on -State-Error.                                     01170099
      *                                                                 01180099
      *      When R791ERRX-State-Error                                  01190099
      *        ...                                                      01200099
      *                                                                 01210099
      *   See alternative 1c...                                         01220099
      *                                                                 01230099
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*01240099
      * Alt 2c: State-Error upon return from a sub-program,             01250099
      *         where R7919999 is used:                                 01260099
      *                                                                 01270099
      *   Error situations is handled exactly the same way as abend     01280099
      *   situations, except that instead of testing on -State-Abend,   01290099
      *   you test on -State-Error.                                     01300099
      *                                                                 01310099
      *      When R7919999-Return-Error                                 01320099
      *        ...                                                      01330099
      *                                                                 01340099
      *   See alternative 1d...                                         01350099
      *                                                                 01360099
      *----------------------------------------------------------------*01370099
      * The Error Handling may display error information and produce    01380099
      * a user abend in batch.                                          01390099
      * In CICS, the error information will be written to the CICS log, 01400099
      * but it will not produce an abend in CICS.                       01410099
      * To trigger this, you need to set this code:                     01420099
      *                                                                 01430099
      *    Set   R791ERR0-In-User-Abend  To    True                     01440099
      *                                                                 01450099
      *################################################################*01460099
